 :proposed-contract {:input "One explicitly synthetic non-secret fixture string and a separately provisioned expected source identity, never a profile, path, environment, executable or policy. Identity cannot be selected or made trusted by the artifact or request. Closed records reject missing, extra and wrongly typed fields."
                     :octets "Bytes are portable persistent vectors of integers 0..255, not strings, JS typed arrays, signed byte arrays or lazy sequences. Validate type, every octet and vector count before decoding, hashing or parsing. Pure strict UTF-8 decoding rejects overlong sequences, isolated continuations, truncated multibyte sequences, encoded surrogate scalars and scalars above U+10FFFF; re-encode decoded string with oikos.law.digest/utf8 and require exact original vector equality. Paired UTF-16 high/low surrogates encode as one scalar; isolated high or low surrogates reject on both BB and NBB. Never substitute replacement characters."
                     :limits {:value-utf8-bytes 32768 :payload-utf8-bytes 65536 :descriptor-utf8-bytes 65536
                              :law "All limits inclusive. Independently count UTF-8 bytes for the input value, entire rendered EDN payload including fixed key, quotes, escapes and LF, and entire JSON descriptor including keys, punctuation and escaped value. Use bounded incremental/preflight counting before building the complete output; stop on overrun and do not truncate. Escape expansion can cause a valid value to exceed either final-byte ceiling. At validation independently bound raw vectors before decoding and decoded value before re-rendering."
                              :grounding "At d4f6ff scripts/local_generation_fs.py permits policy max_file_bytes at most 1048576 and tests both raw payload and raw descriptor individually against policy max_file_bytes and their aggregate against max_total_bytes; policy may be tighter. wire.decode defaults to 16777216 bytes for descriptor JSON. The standalone 65536 ceilings are stronger consumer limits, not evidence of an actual policy, aggregate allowance or full adapter compatibility; later owner policy can still reject. The 131072 stdout bound elsewhere is not an artifact file limit."}
                     :payload "Canonical UTF-8 EDN exactly {:fixture/value <quoted-string>} followed by exactly one LF. Fixed keyword and spacing; use S1A generation/canonical for this closed map only after validating the bounded value. String escapes use quote/backslash, b/f/n/r/t and lowercase four-digit Unicode escapes for other controls; other valid Unicode scalars are emitted literally without normalization. NUL and unpaired surrogates reject even if escaped; no slash escape, BOM, alternate whitespace, metadata, tags, additional keys or forms. Use bounded frame/read-one only after strict decoding and compare parsed closed shape plus exact re-rendered octets; never ambient read-string or eval."
                     :descriptor "Canonical descriptor is raw UTF-8 JSON octets, not EDN or the development handoff descriptor: exactly {\"schema\":\"services.inert-edn/v1\",\"value\":<quoted-string>} with no BOM, extra whitespace or newline, keys in that fixed order and the same canonical JSON-compatible string escaping as payload. Its decoded value equals payload value. A restricted dedicated pure parser or closed deterministic recognizer in the same namespace validates the exact canonical descriptor; it cannot invoke an ambient JSON/EDN evaluator or accept duplicate/extra keys. This is a proposed byte representation, not evidence it has been executed against Services."
                     :pin "The externally provisioned expected closed identity is {:services-repository \"open-hax/services\", :artifact-commit \"d4f6ff570c7b8d2921bdf1a854c521681c96ff6b\", :artifact-tree \"d54a348e1346fec8230b09a8dd6e1c0eba6aae88\", :runtime-commit \"b2973ef9e3246522324dec4658fbeb093ffab147\", :runtime-tree \"daf053cce6b24c8d62f59e660b90b6c92a5bbae2\", :validator-source-sha256 \"0c6396e4db4e55b41fe374f5c7e30a6cde4733e06c689e52d229e23e6a513201\", :wire-source-sha256 \"5572912fd4bec1e738d205818bb991899704ea8a7dd77b6a24ebd120ed8f55f6\", :handoff-descriptor-sha256 \"4aeba4c203db2fe3347021713390f5f0b81a251f14477dc51ad4ceeaa108ecb8\", :adapter-id :oikos/services-inert-edn-adapter-v1, :adapter-revision <externally qualified lowercase sha256>, :validator-id :oikos/services-inert-edn-validator-v1, :validator-revision <externally qualified lowercase sha256>}. Both Oikos revision values are separately provisioned after exact-source review; no invented revision, no requirement to embed a file's own hash in itself. Exact key set, constants, valid digest shapes and equality to the separately trusted expected record are mandatory. Artifact values alone cannot grant trust; static comparison neither authenticates source nor verifies bytes. The separate expected record is provided by the future consumer's trusted boundary, never by a candidate artifact."
                     :errors "Closed sanitized fixed-code errors, no input/value echo; no fallback to profile renderer, bash, host environment, network or process. No approval, authority or effect inferred from success."}
 :artifact-contract {:record "Closed standalone {:schema :oikos/services-inert-artifact-v1, :format :services/inert-edn-v1, :payload-bytes [octet ...], :payload-byte-count integer, :payload-sha256 lowercase-sha256, :descriptor-bytes [octet ...], :descriptor-byte-count integer, :descriptor-sha256 lowercase-sha256, :source-binding <closed identity above>}. No other fields; it is not an S1A target, Services manifest, Services policy FormatBinding, generation, destination, approval or attestation."
                     :hash-law "For each vector, strict UTF-8 decode and exact digest/utf8 round-trip first. Then digest/sha256(decoded-string) is exactly SHA-256 of the original octets because equality was established; count is vector count. Reject any mismatch independently for payload and descriptor. Never hash replacement-decoded text or a printed byte vector. No artifact self-hash and no generation-level digest are defined; defer any such identity to separately reviewed later design."
                     :independent-validation "Consumer validates closed record and independently supplied expected binding afresh, bounds and validates both byte vectors, byte counts and hashes, decodes strictly, checks closed payload and descriptor grammars, reconstructs exact canonical bytes and proves the two decoded values equal. Repeat at the later outer consumer boundary immediately before any trusted policy/facade handoff; this plan does not implement that boundary. Do not trust the producer's success flag, artifact-supplied identity or a digest as proof of intent. Actual owner source/interpreter/policy bytes and admitted fixture remain a separate future trust and compatibility gate."
                     :independence "Separate render and validate entry points; validation recomputes relationships from independently received artifact octets and external expected identity, rather than accepting producer-calculated booleans. Exact independent Services-validator behavior is separately gated; this is not a copied Services validator or proof of all Services inputs."}
 :red-oracles [{:id :r01 :test "Before source exists, shared BB and NBB test requires synthetic value lambda to yield exact UTF-8 {:fixture/value \"lambda\"} plus LF and closed descriptor schema/value; verify exact bytes and digest in both runtimes."}
               {:id :r02 :test "Independently validate correct bytes and descriptor; reject different values, wrong schema, missing/extra descriptor keys, non-string value, Oikos profile projection, missing or substituted binding and wrong validator/wire/source revision."}
               {:id :r03 :test "Reject duplicate keys, second form, tags, metadata, reader eval, extra fields, malformed/truncated UTF-8, BOM, trailing junk, wrong final LF, escaped slash, alternate whitespace and wrong raw byte/hash even if a general parser returns a map. No evaluation."}
               {:id :r04 :test "Check quote, backslash, control escapes, Unicode and non-BMP canonical goldens, plus invalid surrogate, NUL, oversize and malformed descriptor; descriptor/payload mismatch always rejects. Never stringify arbitrary input or leak it in failures."}
               {:id :r05 :test "Pure execution has no environment, filesystem, clock, process, service, network, policy or authorization dependency; unavailable binding has explicit failure and no fallback. S1A existing EDN success, Bash unavailable and existing protocol tests remain unchanged and green."}
               {:id :r06 :test "Under separately granted later admission only, compare exact adapter bytes and closed descriptor against the exact pinned Services validator, including positive and adversarial vectors, then separately review trusted policy FormatBinding, actual interpreter hash, source bytes, fd-3 launch and private fixture before any effect test. A pure unit test or copied validator is not this proof."}
               {:id :r07 :test "For a known valid closed artifact independently mutate each field, each nested source-binding field, schema, format, both byte counts and both digests; independently add/remove keys at both levels. Alter payload and descriptor bytes separately, then also recompute corresponding hashes/counts and retain mismatched intent: every case rejects. Changing both artifact binding and renderer-supplied expected binding cannot establish trust; only independent approved binding qualifies. No self-hash or implied generation hash."}
               {:id :r08 :test "On both runtimes test octet vector domain, invalid raw payload and descriptor vectors, overlong ASCII and multibyte encodings, isolated continuations, truncation, surrogate-encoded scalars, >U+10FFFF and malformed descriptor bytes; require strict rejection before parse/hash. Paired non-BMP scalar exact byte goldens pass; isolated host-string surrogates reject. Assert digest on accepted exact raw vectors and independently established SHA-256 goldens."}
               {:id :r09 :test "On both runtimes exercise value UTF-8 byte lengths 32767, 32768 and 32769; payload and descriptor lengths 65535, 65536 and 65537 via deterministic values when constructible within other bounds. Test each boundary with independent exact octet fixtures and test escape-expanded values that meet input bound but exceed payload or descriptor bound. If a precise boundary is unreachable under the other ceiling, prove that constraint with a reachable nearest case and exercise the raw-vector bound separately. No excessive construction or truncation."}
               {:id :r10 :test "Descriptor exact JSON octets, independently calculated descriptor SHA-256 and equality against payload; reject schema substitution, changed values, extra/duplicate keys, noncanonical JSON escapes or whitespace and stale digest. Prove later consumer independently revalidates; no future facade invocation is performed in the source-only tests."}]
